# WebSockets (D106) without a server: a connection that is refused, the
# states and properties of a socket, and what the statements refuse.
connect to websocket "ws://127.0.0.1:1/chat" using protocol "chat" and call it socket
say "state:" state of socket
say "url:" url of socket
say "protocol:" protocol of socket
say socket
if socket is connecting
    say "it is connecting"
.
if not socket is open
    say "it is not open yet"
.
on open of socket
    say "opened, which should not happen"
.
on error of socket
    say "an error arrived"
.
on close of socket
    say "closed with code" close code "clean:" close was clean
    say "state now:" state of socket
    if socket is closed
        say "it is closed"
    .
.
try
    send "hello" through socket
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    say received message
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    say close code
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    say close reason
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    say close was clean
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    say websocket error
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    connect to websocket 42 and call it other
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    connect to websocket "http://example.test" and call it other
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    connect to websocket "ws://127.0.0.1:1" using protocol 7 and call it other
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
